---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Contact | ${SITE.name}`}
  description="How to report an error in a calculator, suggest a tool, or get in touch."
  crumbs={[{ label: 'Contact' }]}
  noAds
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="tool-header">
      <h1>Contact</h1>
      <p class="tool-standfirst">
        Corrections are the most useful thing you can send us. They get fixed the same day.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="tool-body">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
        </p>

        <h2>Reporting an error</h2>
        <p>
          If a figure looks wrong, the fastest way to get it fixed is to send us:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>The calculator, and ideally the URL — inputs are saved in the address bar, so copying it captures your exact figures.</li>
          <li>The number we gave you.</li>
          <li>The number you expected, and where it came from.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We check every report against the primary source. If we are wrong we fix it that day and
          record it on the <a href="/changelog/">changelog</a>. If we are right, we will explain why
          — often it turns out to be a genuine subtlety worth adding to the page.
        </p>

        <h2>Suggesting a calculator</h2>
        <p>
          Tell us what you were trying to work out and why the existing tools did not help. The most
          useful suggestions describe a real situation rather than a feature.
        </p>

        <h2>What we cannot do</h2>
        <p>
          We cannot give tax advice or comment on your personal circumstances. We are not accountants
          and are not regulated to advise. For your own affairs, speak to a qualified accountant, to
          HMRC, or to one of the free services listed on our{' '}
          <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer page</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Using our content</h2>
        <p>
          Quoting our figures with a link back is welcome. If you write about UK tax and want to
          reference a calculator, or think one would be useful to your readers, do get in touch.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
